                                    <li>Death certificate - Notarized/Attested by a gazetted officer</li>
                                    <li>F.I.R - Notarized/Attested by a gazetted officer</li>
                                    <li>Police Final charge sheet/Court Final order - Notarized/Attested by a Gazetted Officer - if applicable </li>
                                    <li>Spot and/or Inquest Panchnama - Notarized/Attested by a gazetted officer</li>
                                    <li>Post Mortem Report - Notarized/Attested by a gazetted officer</li>
                                    <li>Viscera Analysis Report/Chemical analysis report/Forensic Science Lab report - If applicable - Notarized/Attested by gazetted officer</li>
                                    <li>Other Document as per Case details - Copy of Treatment papers; if hospitalized, Website Links/Newspaper cuttings, other references</li>
                                    <li>If the claim amount is more than <span class="rpicon">`</span> 1 Lakh, AML Documents - Pan Card Copy, Residence Proof, 2 Passport size colour photos of claimant</li>
                                    <li>Cancelled Cheque with NEFT Mandate form - duly filled in by the claimant and bank</li>
                                    <li>Any other document as required by the Company or Company's TPA to investigate the claim or our obligation to make payment for it</li>
                                </ul></br>
                             <p class="answer">Permanent Total Disablement (PTD) due to accident</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>PA Claim form duly filled &amp; signed by the Insured/Claimant</li>
                                    <li>Policy Copy</li>
                                    <li>MLC OR F.I.R.OR PANCHNAMA- Notarised/Attested by a gazetted officer</li>
                                    <li>Disability Certificate issued by Authorised civil surgeon- Original/Notarised/Attested by a gazetted officer</li>
                                    <li>Treatment papers, X-rays films/laboratory test reports and other diagnostic reports to support the claim and percentage of disability</li>
                                    <li>Medical report</li>
                                    <li>Colour Photograph of the injured reflecting disability</li>
                                    <li>If the claim amount is more than <span class="rpicon">`</span> 1 Lakh, AML Documents - Pan Card Copy, Residence Proof, 2 Passport size colour photos of claimant</li>
                                    <li>Other Document as per Case details - Copy of Treatment papers; if hospitalised, Website Links/Newspaper cuttings, other references</li>
                                    <li>Cancelled Cheque with NEFT Mandate form - duly filled in by the claimant</li>
                                    <li>Any other document as required by the Company or Company's TPA to investigate the claim or our obligation to make payment for it</li>
                                </ul></br>
                              <p class="answer">Accidental Hospitalisation Reimbursement Expenses</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>Policy copy</li>
                                    <li>Claim form duly filled &amp; signed by the claimant</li>
                                    <li>F.I.R. and Panchnama wherever applicable (original or certified copies)</li>
                                    <li>Medical &amp; Investigation report</li>
                                    <li>Prescriptions</li>
                                    <li>Medical &amp; Investigation Bills</li>
                                    <li>Discharge Card</li>
                                    <li>If claim amount is more than <span class="rpicon">`</span> 1 Lakh, AML Documents - Pan Card Copy, Residence Proof, 2 Passport size colour photos of claimant</li>
                                    <li>Cancelled Cheque and NEFT Mandate form - duly filled in by the claimant</li>
                                    <li>Any other document as required by the Company or Company's TPA to investigate the claim or our obligation to make payment for it</li>
                                </ul></br>
                                 <p class="answer">Accidental Hospital Daily allowance</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li>All documents related to Death/PTD/PPD/TTD, as the case may be</li>
                                    <li>Discharge Card</li>
                                    <li>If claim amount is more than <span class="rpicon">`</span> 1 Lakh, AML Documents - Pan Card Copy, Residence Proof, 2 Passport size colour photos of claimant</li>
                                    <li>Cancelled Cheque and NEFT Mandate form - duly filled in by the claimant</li>
                                    <li>Any other document as required by the Company or Company's TPA to investigate the claim or our obligation to make payment for it</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <div class="qustAnswrBox">
                                <h5 class="question">What is the procedure for making a claim?</h5>
                                <p class="answer">In case of a claim, please follow the following procedures:</p>
                                <ul>
                                    <li> Log the claim by calling our toll free number at 1800 2666 or email us at <a href="mailto:customersupport@icicilombard.com">customersupport@icicilombard.com</a></li>
                                    <li>You may also log a claim by giving immediate notice in writing to the Company</li>
                                     <p class="answer">Write to the following address to log the claim:
                                    <br /> Individual Personal Accident Claims Manager
                                    <br /> Retail Claims,
                                    <br /> ICICI Lombard Healthcare,
                                    <br /> Varun Tower II, 1st, 4th, 5th & 6th Floor, 
                                    <br /> Begumpet, Hyderabad, 
                                    <br /> Telangana, Pin code – 500016.
                                    </p>
                                    <li>We will then guide you on the further steps to take.</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <a href="/info-center/faqs?page=Personal Protect&amp;tab=tab-general" class="readMore">Read All FAQs</a>
                        </div>
                        <div class="tabCnt active">
                            <div class="qustAnswrBox">
                                <h3 class="question">  What is the age limit for taking this policy?</h3>
                                <p class="answer">The entry age of the insured is 5 years, however the proposer (Parents/Legal guardian/s) should be atleast 18 years of age. There is Lifelong Renewability under the policy.</p>
                            </div>
                            <a href="/info-center/faqs?page=Personal Protect&amp;tab=tab-general" class="readMore">Read All FAQs</a>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div> -->
</div>
