{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FinancialProduct",
  "name": "Personal Accident Insurance",
  "description": "Personal Accident Insurance: Our PA insurance policy provides financial security for you & your family in case of disability or death.",
  "offers": {
    "@type": "Offer",
    "offeredBy": "https://www.icicilombard.com/health-insurance/personal-accident-insurance"
  }
}
</script>



<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is Personal Protect policy?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "ICICI Lombard Personal Protect policy provides your beneficiary with a death benefit in the unfortunate event of your accidental death. It also provides you with cover against Permanent Total Disablement (PTD) on account of an accident. Optional coverage can also be offered against Accidental Hospitalisation Expenses Reimbursement and Accidental Hospital Daily Allowance."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What are the benefits of Personal Protect Policy?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "With Personal Protect policy, you can avail the following benefits:

Cover against Accidental Death or Permanent Total Disablement (PTD) on account of an Accident
Optional cover against Accidental Hospitalisation Expenses and Accidental Hospital Daily Allowance
No health check-up required
Easy Claim Process with minimal documentation
Digitally signed policy available 24X7 online"
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What covers does the Personal Protect Policy offer?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "The Personal Protect plan covers against:

Death due to an accident
Permanent Total Disablement (PTD) due to an accident
Optional cover:

Accidental Hospitalisation Expenses
Accidental Hospital Daily Allowance
Now choose between 6 easy Personal Protect plans to insure your personal safety available in ` 3 Lakh, `5 Lakh, ` 10 Lakh, ` 15 Lakh, ` 20 Lakh and ` 25 Lakh cover options."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Can I take cover for my spouse?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, you can buy an additional policy cover for your spouse aged between 18-65years."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What are your Premium rates?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "The premium rates are based on the sum insured opted for, the coverage selected and the tenure of the policy. You can calculate the premium using our calculators."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What are the different modes of payment?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Now you can choose between 5 payment options to pay your premium online:

Credit Card – Make secure premium payments with your VISA, Master and AMEX card. Avail EMI too.
Net banking - Transfer premium amounts online through ICICI Bank and 9 other select banks
Bill Pay – Use your ICICI Bank Internet Banking account to pay your insurance premium
Debit Card – Just enter your Citibank Debit Card details to pay your insurance premium directly
Cash Card - Use your Done Card to make payment online."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What are the different modes of payment?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Please refer the rate chart for checking premium for this policy"
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Whom do I have to contact in case of a claim?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "In case of a claim, you can call our toll free number at 1800 2666, alternatively mail us at customersupport@icicilombard.com"
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Which documents are needed to make a claim?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "The documents required for processing a claim are as follows:
Accidental Death

PA Claim form duly filled & signed by the nominee
Policy Copy
Death certificate - Notarized/Attested by a gazetted officer
F.I.R - Notarized/Attested by a gazetted officer
Police Final charge sheet/Court Final order - Notarized/Attested by a Gazetted Officer - if applicable
Spot and/or Inquest Panchnama - Notarized/Attested by a gazetted officer
Post Mortem Report - Notarized/Attested by a gazetted officer
Viscera Analysis Report/Chemical analysis report/Forensic Science Lab report - If applicable - Notarized/Attested by gazetted officer
Other Document as per Case details - Copy of Treatment papers; if hospitalized, Website Links/Newspaper cuttings, other references
If the claim amount is more than ` 1 Lakh, AML Documents - Pan Card Copy, Residence Proof, 2 Passport size colour photos of claimant
Cancelled Cheque with NEFT Mandate form - duly filled in by the claimant and bank
Any other document as required by the Company or Company's TPA to investigate the claim or our obligation to make payment for it

Permanent Total Disablement (PTD) due to accident

PA Claim form duly filled & signed by the Insured/Claimant
Policy Copy
MLC OR F.I.R.OR PANCHNAMA- Notarised/Attested by a gazetted officer
Disability Certificate issued by Authorised civil surgeon- Original/Notarised/Attested by a gazetted officer
Treatment papers, X-rays films/laboratory test reports and other diagnostic reports to support the claim and percentage of disability
Medical report
Colour Photograph of the injured reflecting disability
If the claim amount is more than ` 1 Lakh, AML Documents - Pan Card Copy, Residence Proof, 2 Passport size colour photos of claimant
Other Document as per Case details - Copy of Treatment papers; if hospitalised, Website Links/Newspaper cuttings, other references
Cancelled Cheque with NEFT Mandate form - duly filled in by the claimant
Any other document as required by the Company or Company's TPA to investigate the claim or our obligation to make payment for it

Accidental Hospitalisation Reimbursement Expenses

Policy copy
Claim form duly filled & signed by the claimant
F.I.R. and Panchnama wherever applicable (original or certified copies)
Medical & Investigation report
Prescriptions
Medical & Investigation Bills
Discharge Card
If claim amount is more than ` 1 Lakh, AML Documents - Pan Card Copy, Residence Proof, 2 Passport size colour photos of claimant
Cancelled Cheque and NEFT Mandate form - duly filled in by the claimant
Any other document as required by the Company or Company's TPA to investigate the claim or our obligation to make payment for it

Accidental Hospital Daily allowance

All documents related to Death/PTD/PPD/TTD, as the case may be
Discharge Card
If claim amount is more than ` 1 Lakh, AML Documents - Pan Card Copy, Residence Proof, 2 Passport size colour photos of claimant
Cancelled Cheque and NEFT Mandate form - duly filled in by the claimant
Any other document as required by the Company or Company's TPA to investigate the claim or our obligation to make payment for it"
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is the procedure for making a claim?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "In case of a claim, please follow the following procedures:

Log the claim by calling our toll free number at 1800 2666 or email us at customersupport@icicilombard.com
You may also log a claim by giving immediate notice in writing to the Company
Write to the following address to log the claim:
Individual Personal Accident Claims Manager
Retail Claims,
ICICI Lombard Healthcare,
ICICI Bank Tower, Plot No. 12 Financial District,
Nanakram Guda, Gachibowli, Hyderabad,
Andhra Pradesh, Pin Code: 500032

We will then guide you on the further steps to take."
    }
  },{
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "What is the age limit for taking this policy?",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "The entry age of the insured is 5 years, however the proposer (Parents/Legal guardian/s) should be atleast 18 years of age. There is Lifelong Renewability under the policy."
    }
  }]
}
</script>


